h T2-T4 exposed, it's less useful for chows. Alternatively, discard T7 or T8. But T7 and T8 might combine with T9 for a terminal chow (7-8-9), which could be worth Two Terminal Chows (1 point) if I form another. However, I only have one T7 and one T8, so I'd need to draw more.\n\nConsidering efficiency, I should discard the tile with the fewest possible combinations. T3 has no adjacent tiles in my hand (T7 is far away). W8 is also isolated. I'll discard T3 to keep the B4 triplet and honor pair.\n\nAnswer: Play T3"}
